From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] configs: orangepi_zero2: scan the six USB host controllers in parallel

With the on-board USB-A port and the two expansion-board ports enabled
the Zero2 has three EHCI and three OHCI root hubs, and the sequential
bus scan in "usb start" (preboot) costs the 1 s connect debounce per
controller: 7 s with nothing plugged in, up from 2.5 s with one port.
Enable CONFIG_UTHREAD so usb_init() initialises and scans the
controllers in parallel (together with the usb_hub yield fix) which
brings the scan back to roughly the two-port figure while keeping every
port bootable.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig
+++ b/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig
@@ -29,3 +29,4 @@
 CONFIG_USB_OHCI_HCD=y
 CONFIG_USB_MUSB_GADGET=y
 # CONFIG_USB_ETHER is not set
+CONFIG_UTHREAD=y
